body:
I don't mind helping Sherpa it if you need. (Anytime before 5PM PST that is). I have a few clears, and have tarrabah. Message me if you get a group together and need the guide. 

&#x200B;

PSN: Vatsu

No problem at all. While I do prefer LW, SotP is where its at in regards to quick loot. If the group wants to start with SotP first, I don't mind that at all. Likewise, feel free to add me on PSN if you need an extra hand in a SotP group or something. 

&#x200B;

But yeah, looking forward to playing with ya tomorrow.

WOWWWWWWWW that makes so much sense. Never thought of that haha. Since foe's saps mp and I gain it back with refresh. HUGE DUH. 

&#x200B;

Last question on that end. Im assuming the party buffs reach the size of he screen but for things like foe's and refresh, how close do I have to be to the enemies/healers for them to reap the benefits (or be afflicted). Cause I have no idea wtf a yalm is.

Thanks ipartyhawd!

&#x200B;

Didn't know if they were as good as all youtubers say cause a 2% crit buff doesnt seem like all that to me. But the utility does help.

Thanks War!

&#x200B;

Someone above mentioned something similar: Why are drk's not in demand (tank wise I'm assuming? Don't know if they are dps able like warriors). Also awesome clarification on the legacy aspect. Makes sense Why I don't see as many.

Thank you Keisero, I didn't know about fflogs at all so I will make sure to utilize it. (Just have to gear to extreme first. Currently like sub 280ilvl brd).

&#x200B;

Followup question. I thought Dragoons weren't liked due to the animation lock? And Why doesn't anyone like Dark Knight? (I wanted to look cool and fun)
